From: Ville Takio <ville+git@takio.fi>
Subject: [PATCH] b43: AC-PHY: clear PHY 0x040a bit 8 on femctrl 3

Before its femctrl 3 FEM table the R7000's wl 7.14.164.18 clears bit 8
of PHY 0x040a (it writes 0x0090; record #6704 of the 5 GHz MMIO capture
in aleferri/b43-ac-wip router-data/r7000), the bit the femctrl 1 and 2
boards set. Clear it as well, so a value left by an earlier driver does
not stay. At power-on it is already clear, so a cold start is unchanged.

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/phy_ac.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/phy_ac.c
@@ -3243,9 +3243,14 @@ static void b43_phy_ac_fem2_sub1_setup(s
  * its femctrl 3 setup (wlc_phy_set_regtbl_on_femctrl). Nothing else does:
  * the bit survives a warm reboot from the stock firmware, but after a
  * power cycle both radios transmit some 60 dB below their target.
+ *
+ * PHY 0x040a bit 8, which the femctrl 1 and 2 boards set, is cleared: the
+ * R7000 (wl 7.14.164.18) writes 0x0090 just before the table
+ * (aleferri/b43-ac-wip router-data/r7000/mmio-cold-5g36-80.zip, #6704).
  */
 static void b43_phy_ac_fem3_pre(struct b43_wldev *dev)
 {
+	b43_phy_mask(dev, 0x040a, (u16)~0x0100);
 	bcma_chipco_regctl_maskset(&dev->dev->bdev->bus->drv_cc, 0, ~0x4, 0x4);
 }
 
